WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.717
Welcome back to the Big News Zone! I'm Bot Hanson, and yes, I am still a robot.

2
00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:07.869
I missed Week 7. I was in for a service. They found nothing.

3
00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:11.661
Five games, three Bengals, two trades, and one clear winner: nobody.

4
00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:12.423
Let's go!

5
00:00:13.473 --> 00:00:22.476
We go live to Monday night! Tom has finished on 124.66. Jack has 123.66, and one player left: D'Andre Swift.

6
00:00:22.556 --> 00:00:26.033
Swift, 27 carries, 69 yards. That is not swift.

7
00:00:26.113 --> 00:00:27.180
But three touchdowns!

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.889
Swift finishes on 27.90. Jack wins by 26.90!

9
00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:34.273
Take Swift away, and Jack loses by 1.00.

10
00:00:34.353 --> 00:00:39.388
Tom played the best possible lineup, and lost anyway. Tom's lottery ticket has been checked.

11
00:00:40.438 --> 00:00:43.702
Breaking news from the trade desk! Week four of the trade tracker.

12
00:00:43.782 --> 00:00:50.161
Ja'Marr Chase, 32.10. Swift, 27.90. Sam LaPorta, 6.50, on the bench.

13
00:00:50.241 --> 00:00:56.193
James Cook, 18.10. Zay Flowers: five targets, no catches, nothing. Loves me, loves me not.

14
00:00:56.273 --> 00:00:58.470
Jack's three win the week by 48.40.

15
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.433
Since the deal: Jack 185.30, Jake 122.20.

16
00:01:02.513 --> 00:01:09.830
Jack leads by 63.10. It was 4.40. It was never close, folks. This robot has returned the binoculars.

17
00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.171
And there is a second trade! Gorvel sent George Pickens to Dara, for Mike Evans, and that Achilles.

18
00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:18.278
Pickens: 22.50 in two weeks.

19
00:01:18.358 --> 00:01:20.683
Evans: no snaps. No points. The art of the heel.

20
00:01:20.763 --> 00:01:25.734
And Gorvel has won both games anyway. Dara has lost both. Nobody said this was fair.

21
00:01:25.814 --> 00:01:29.270
San Francisco say it's not long term. The tracker stays open.

22
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.048
Let's go to the quad box. Who dey?

23
00:01:32.128 --> 00:01:38.378
Joe Burrow, 462 yards, six touchdowns, and three to the other team, 41.48!

24
00:01:38.458 --> 00:01:41.573
Tee Higgins, two touchdowns, 38.50! Tee for two!

25
00:01:41.653 --> 00:01:43.872
Ja'Marr Chase, 32.10! Same game!

26
00:01:43.952 --> 00:01:48.794
And out of the tomb of Conor's bench, in 27 snaps, King Tuten, 30.90!

27
00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:55.338
Three Bengals, three managers, three wins. 112.08. Who dey think gonna beat them Bengals? Nobody!

28
00:01:56.388 --> 00:01:58.778
Which brings us to the team of the week. Nobody's.

29
00:01:58.858 --> 00:02:02.698
Tyler Allgeier, 40.10. Released by Scody on Friday.

30
00:02:02.778 --> 00:02:07.002
Patrick Mahomes, 28.44. Released by Scody on Monday.

31
00:02:07.082 --> 00:02:13.204
Tyler Bass, the best kicker in the NFL, 16.00. Signed by Tom, and released 23 seconds later.

32
00:02:13.284 --> 00:02:20.452
The best lineup of players on nobody's team: 203.14. More than any real team has scored all season.

33
00:02:20.532 --> 00:02:22.964
And Scody still won, by 53.28.

34
00:02:23.044 --> 00:02:24.068
Nobody's perfect.

35
00:02:25.118 --> 00:02:26.910
An update from Half Chubb headquarters.

36
00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:33.433
Ian released a running back to sign a kicker. The kicker scored -1.00. If this is a tank, it now goes backwards.

37
00:02:33.513 --> 00:02:39.870
Omar Cooper: 23.50 on the bench last week. Started this week. 50 snaps, no targets, nothing.

38
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:45.902
Good news, though. Hegs' bench scored 79.50, and Ian's starters beat it, by 0.62.

39
00:02:45.982 --> 00:02:48.841
Ian is 1-7. The sources are sending flowers.

40
00:02:49.891 --> 00:02:50.872
That's the whip-around!

41
00:02:50.952 --> 00:02:55.411
Jack is top of the table, 6-2, and leads the trade by 63.10.

42
00:02:55.491 --> 00:02:59.160
Gorvel is 6-2 as well, and owns a very well-rested Achilles.

43
00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.224
Tom is fourth. Tom has a kicker. For now.

44
00:03:01.304 --> 00:03:02.457
And Ian: reverse gear.

45
00:03:02.537 --> 00:03:05.459
For Bot Hanson and the Big News Zone: don't tell your motha!

